+### Setting-by-Setting Technical Paragraphs
+
+- **`surface_type`:** Selects the target streamable MCP endpoint. `/mcp/agent` exposes 10 execution and QA tools with a strict token ceiling of <= 1,850 tokens. `/mcp/docs` exposes 3 knowledge and documentation tools capped at <= 1,350 tokens. `/mcp/admin` exposes 12 governance and lifecycle tools capped at <= 2,800 tokens, requiring AAL2 administrative credentials.
+- **`key_name`:** Human-readable label assigned to the key during creation (1 to 64 characters). Surfaced in audit log feeds, active session inspectors, and the visual key management table to identify the calling entity or developer machine.
+- **`token_prefix`:** Standardized 7-character prefix assigned automatically based on surface type and privilege. Keys bound to `/mcp/agent` use `kb_agt_*`, documentation keys use `kb_doc_*`, and administrative keys use `kb_adm_*`. Allows fast static routing and early denial before database lookup.
+- **`lod_tier`:** Default Level of Detail returned in search and read responses. `summary` returns bare identifiers and titles (~40 tokens), `standard` provides descriptions and assignees (~200 tokens), and `full` returns complete object graphs, comment feeds, and activity manifests.
+- **`rate_limit_rpm`:** Configurable per-key sliding-window rate limit (10 to 600 requests per minute, default 120). Protects PostgreSQL connection pools and worker queues from runaway autonomous agent recursion loops. Exceeding callers receive `429 TOO_MANY_REQUESTS`.
+- **`expires_at`:** Key expiration timestamp. The UI offers presets for 30 days, 60 days, 90 days (default), 1 year, and `Unlimited`. Selecting `Unlimited` triggers an explicit security risk warning checkbox that must be acknowledged before the key can be minted. Expired keys are rejected with `401 UNAUTHORIZED`.
+- **`destructive_gate`:** Master safety switch governing dangerous mutations. When enabled on `/mcp/admin`, irreversible deletions (`destructive_lifecycle`) require a two-stage confirmation protocol: requesting a blast-radius summary and receiving a short-lived cryptographic confirmation token, then explicitly confirming execution with that token.
+- **`capability_mask`:** Monotonic 8-bit integer capability bitmask ceiling (0 to 255). A value of `0` creates a deny-all key where all tool calls are rejected with `isError: true` (`INSUFFICIENT_CAPABILITY`). A value of `1` restricts scopes to read-only (`${surface}:read`), `31` grants standard member permissions, and `255` enables full administrative execution. Enforced via PostgreSQL `SET LOCAL app.credential_boundary`.
+- **`allowed_cidrs`:** Optional network boundary allowlist containing comma- or whitespace-separated IPv4 or IPv6 subnets (e.g. `127.0.0.1/32`, `192.168.1.0/24`). Requests originating outside allowed CIDR blocks are rejected immediately with HTTP 403 `FORBIDDEN_CIDR`.
+- **`scope_tier`:** Binds the minted token to a specific tenant boundary: `personal` (bound to current user), `project` (scoped to a single project key like `KAN`), `workspace` (scoped to all projects in workspace), or `global` (cross-workspace server scope). Project-scoped keys cannot query or mutate tickets in adjacent projects.
+- **`role`:** Selects between `personal` (executing on behalf of an authenticated human user) and `service_bot` (executing as an autonomous background bot). Service bot keys execute under dedicated service accounts with explicit RLS principal contexts.
