 ## 2. Role-Bound HKDF-HMAC Internal Service Authentication
@@ -99,6 +101,27 @@ sequenceDiagram
 2. **SSRF-Hardened OpenID Discovery:** Provider discovery and JWKS retrieval reuse the secure discovery client, enforcing private IP address blocking (RFC 1918 / RFC 4193), timeout caps, and response size limits.
 3. **Atomic Replay Prevention:** Each OIDC JWT carries a unique token identifier (`jti`). The server executes an atomic PostgreSQL insert into `workload_jti_replays` (`ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING`). If the same `jti` is submitted a second time, the transaction aborts with `401 WORKLOAD_TOKEN_REPLAYED`.
 4. **Subject Pattern & Claim Filtering:** Workload identity policies define glob patterns for the token subject (`sub`), such as `repo:org/repo:ref:refs/heads/main`, alongside mandatory JSON claim subsets (e.g. `{"environment": "production"}`).
+5. **Token Lifetime Cap:** Workload identity tokens enforce an explicit lifetime ceiling (`max_ttl_seconds <= 86400`, default 3,600 seconds / 1 hour), mitigating credential exposure windows.
+
+### Workload Identity Policy Specification
+
+Policies are managed by administrators via `/api/v1/admin/workload-identities` (requires AAL2):
+
+| Attribute | Type & Validation | Description |
+| :--- | :--- | :--- |
+| `name` | String (1 to 120 chars) | Descriptive policy label displayed in admin lists |
+| `description` | String or `None` | Optional markdown description of workload context |
+| `issuer` | Strict HTTPS URL (1 to 500 chars) | OIDC identity provider issuer URL |
+| `client_id` | String (1 to 255 chars) | Expected audience (`aud`) claim in OIDC token |
+| `subject_pattern` | Glob or Regex (1 to 500 chars) | Matching pattern for token `sub` claim |
+| `required_claims_json` | JSON Object | Exact claims required in the OIDC JWT payload |
+| `surface` | `agent` or `docs` | Target MCP surface granted to the federated token |
+| `scopes` | List of Strings | Allowed OAuth scopes (e.g. `["agent", "read:issues"]`) |
+| `allowed_project_ids` | List of UUIDs or `None` | Restricts token access to specific project IDs |
+| `capability_mask` | Integer (`0` to `255`, default `255`) | Monotonic capability ceiling enforced by RLS |
+| `allowed_cidrs` | List of CIDR Strings or `None` | Restricts token exchange to specific IP subnets |
+| `max_ttl_seconds` | Integer (`60` to `86400`, default `3600`) | Maximum lifespan of issued ephemeral token |
+| `is_enabled` | Boolean (`true` / `false`) | Toggles active status of the workload policy |
 
